{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270535-if-you-have-to-choose-a-splat-which-one-would-you-be","id":1270535,"title":"If you have to choose a Splat. Which one would you be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-25T00:02:14-08:00","id":1270535,"title":"If you have to choose a Splat. Which one would you be?","content":"For living everyday. No mages because that is such an obvious choice.<br /> <br /> Would being a Sin-Eater be a good choice for practical everyday living?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T00:59:26-08:00","id":1270544,"title":"","content":"Uhm. Is this for OWOD or NWOD? It's in the OWOD section, but you mentioned Sin-Eaters..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky","name":"Kalzky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T08:03:39-08:00","id":1270600,"title":"","content":"Silent Strider probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T06:56:44-08:00","id":1270818,"title":"","content":"Son of Ether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T16:35:19-08:00","id":1270973,"title":"","content":"Defender.<br /> <br /> Second choice would probably be Get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T11:03:05-08:00","id":1271502,"title":"","content":"I think the wereravens have it pretty good: they're fera that the werewolves get along with, and they can fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T13:46:22-08:00","id":1271564,"title":"","content":"No mages? I\u2019m gonna play fair and not say \u201cSorcerer\u201d or \u201cKin-folk\u201d because even though it\u2019s technically not a mage, the intent of the question (i.e. which not strictly human splat would you choose to be) is obvious.<br /> <br /> All the other options for \u201cmostly normal\u201d generally have some type of downside to them. Imbued Hunters get voices in their heads that eventually turn them into fanatics. Ghouls are almost certainly blood bound. The new Mummies get Horus\u2019 politics and requirements for rebirth messing up your existence.<br /> <br /> Of all the non-mage/sorcerer options available I think I\u2019d have to choose the Dhampyr. All the benefits of ghouldom with (generally) none of the downsides and subtle enough to slip under the radar entirely if that\u2019s what you wanted to do.<br /> <br /> You\u2019ve got some anger management issues, but generally lower difficulties for the checks and learning some self-control (and spending willpower if you absolutely must) will generally keep those under control. In exchange you get to be immortal, super strong, can figure out the first dot in the other physical disciplines without a tutor, can heal rapidly and boost your physical stats if needed.<br /> <br /> Most importantly, other than a very thin-blooded vampire parent who likely isn\u2019t even in the picture, you\u2019ve got no supernatural politics dragging you down. No werewolf packs or mage societies looking to recruit you into their existential wars. No sires who created you as a political tool.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re no match for other supernaturals really, but if your goal is simply to lead as normal a life as possible, those advantages might be handy from time to time with no meaningful downsides to compensate for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 11-28-2018, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T15:25:50-08:00","id":1271602,"title":"","content":"I would hope to be a vampire. Knowing my luck I'd end up as a fomori because of all the years of wyrm taint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T19:18:13-08:00","id":1271665,"title":"","content":"A Changeling, like a Troll or Autumn Sidhe. Changelings want to be happy and they want to be themselves, even though they are on the brink of depression and amnesia.<br /> <br /> Or if I\u2019m going to make the sacrifice, I\u2019ll be a Garou like a Stargazer or Fenrir, but that is a harsh life of responsibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T19:20:15-08:00","id":1271666,"title":"","content":"Or Yeah an Amenti or Wu Tian are quite positive rolls as well as having super positive forms of immortality. If I\u2019m Amenti I even have the weakest part of my soul inhabited by the strongest part of another soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T16:19:46-08:00","id":1271866,"title":"","content":"Alchemical Exalted. I want to be a City.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T16:07:51-08:00","id":1272063,"title":"","content":"Why no mages?<br /> <br /> Other than a mage, a vampire. Yeah, with all the baggage. Preferably not one of the clans who have drawn the &quot;you can't mingle with society without magic, because you look like something the dog chewed on, or a decaying corpse&quot;. Or a Tremere, if the old clan structure and curse is up.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, for the &quot;why would anyone want to be a blood-sucking undead monster?&quot; I'd just call up Marius from the Anne Rice books and say &quot;fuck you, I don't want to die and I want to see history unfold and all the things humans could come up with, good or bad&quot;. That, and I'm really not a sunshine-loving person, so I could live with that. The thing I'd miss the most probably, is food.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T19:07:41-08:00","id":1272284,"title":"","content":"Sunlight and food are two things the Dhampyr gets to still enjoy while also getting the immortality to see history unfold. The fact that you don\u2019t need to feed to maintain your existence also helps keep you off the radar since you\u2019ll never need to dispose of a corpse if you lose control of your hunger one night.<br /> <br /> Heck as long as it doesn\u2019t instantly kill you, a Dhampyr can bounce back from just about any injury in minutes. They\u2019ll need days to regain the lost \u201cblood\u201d, but if you\u2019re just trying to escape, laying on the ground pretending to be dead/mortally wounded until you can make a break for it when your attacker doesn\u2019t know you can quick heal is actually a solid plan. Plus, you don\u2019t slip into torpor for being out of blood points.<br /> <br /> Honestly, it\u2019s about the subtlest immortal out there. Amenti are a close second, but still have to spend periods of time in the underworld to recharge some of their energies. Vampires and Ghouls need blood from some source or another to maintain themselves. Mages need ever more paradoxical rituals to maintain immortality<br /> <br /> Dhampyrs maintain their immortality and recharge their energies just by getting up in the morning; no odd rituals, long disappearance, supernatural loyalty to a vampire, or never being seen in daylight and having the occasional body from a feed gone bad to clue people in to the fact that you\u2019re an ageless supernatural being who can be stronger, faster and tougher than any mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T09:25:43-08:00","id":1272399,"title":"","content":"Get of Fenris as their caern is like 20 km from my hometownand i quite like and play them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T11:59:24-08:00","id":1272437,"title":"","content":"I'd be pretty okay with being a Tzimisce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T16:29:57-08:00","id":1272484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></di