ance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T15:49:29-08:00","id":1274111,"title":"","content":"Shemsu-Heru, you got to be immortal, really immortal, you got magic powers, you got freedom, so much freedom that most of the splat said &quot;you know, boss? see ya&quot; and were doing their own games while Horus was trying to single-handendly make a battle against Apophis","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T06:23:58-08:00","id":1274704,"title":"","content":"I'd be a Bone Gnawer. No tough politics to worry about, I get to raid McDonalds for a living, beer flows aplenty and I get the thumbs up from my relatives for whatever childbearing relationship I enter!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24271-froggo","name":"Froggo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24271_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T17:05:17-08:00","id":1284418,"title":"","content":"Hmmmmm, I think I'd be a Fallen if they're a valid choice. I mean, of course, in that I would be the fallen not the hollowed out mortal shell inhabited by one.<br /> <br /> Maybe a Lammasu or Namaru? I'm a little rusty on demon, only got back into it yesterday so if there are any glaringly horrible downsides I'm not aware of them yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6149-malfean90","name":"Malfean90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T09:11:18-08:00","id":1284515,"title":"","content":"I would want to be one of the Amenti, Myself. I favour the Kher-minu and the Sefekhi; if such were real, I'd probably be more likely to wind up as the former rather than the later. As for My faction, I would almost certainly not go with either the Shemsu-heru or the Spiders of the Sands. I'd most likely be independent, but working for the Ashukhi Corporation wouldn't be out of the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T13:29:46-08:00","id":1284562,"title":"","content":"Torn between Devil Tiger and Song Of Shadows Dharma. Or go completely nuts and be the only Dhampire Shih hunter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T23:05:29-08:00","id":1284669,"title":"","content":"D&amp;D - Dragons were presented in one book as how to be playable. Go gold - Polymorph at will, and Wish at will.<br /> <br /> WoD - Dhampir and Revenant would be interesting, but Vampires all the way. Immortality, some pseudo magic, best desiged for manipulating mortals to your bidding.<br /> Easy Dietary requirements FTW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T11:21:41-08:00","id":1284771,"title":"","content":"Can I be one of those anime guys who finds himself in a fantasy world as a completely overpowered godlike being? Because that sounds kind of fun.<br /> <br /> More seriously, if I was a Scion, I think I'd want to be a Scion of Hestia, and aspire to being the God of Minding My Own Business. That, or of Home Cooking.<br /> <br /> If I had to be a vampire, Ventrue maybe.<br /> <br /> Bastet might be interesting, though I'd probably turn into the equivalent of one of those super fat and lazy house cats. <br /> <br /> I aspire to join the Iron Legion, but would probably end up in the Emerald or Skeletal Legions. <br /> <br /> And I'm torn between Boggin or Troll. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 02-04-2019, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T17:09:41-08:00","id":1285081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270535-if-you-have-to-choose-a-splat-which-one-would-you-be?p=1284771#post1284771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I be one of those anime guys who finds himself in a fantasy world as a completely overpowered godlike being? Because that sounds kind of fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Becoming a completely overpowered superbeing in an alternate fantasy world might be fun, but it could also be a huge hassle. Think of all the bureaucratic management a demon \u00fcberlord has to juggle (Ainz Ool Gown), and if you're just trying to live a quiet, peaceful life, people will be coming from the four corners of the world to challenge you (Rimuru Tempest). It might actually be more fun to take the route Kazuma takes in &quot;Konosuba.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270535-if-you-have-to-choose-a-splat-which-one-would-you-be?p=1284771#post1284771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bastet might be interesting, though I'd probably turn into the equivalent of one of those super fat and lazy house cats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that right there could be a pretty sweet life! The trick would be staying unnoticed by the Garou, because once they found you, they'd get all up in your face and try to make you work for a living. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T12:27:59-08:00","id":1285635,"title":"","content":"Genetically Shadow lord or Silver fang or Get of Fenris. First two I would fit as ahroun, for the get, as retribution-like philodox.<br /> <br /> A gangrel or a tzimisce , or maybe brujah, would probably choose me as childe.<br /> <br /> As Imbued, I would be without doubts an Avenger ( both because of my attitude toward life and also because of my passion for physical training and military-martial arts path) with a dangerous attitude ( on the player guide, I would risk to become wayward).<br /> <br /> I don't like mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 02-07-2019, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T16:06:03-08:00","id":1286041,"title":"","content":"Either a Glass Walker or Child of Gaia. Glass Walkers appeal to my love of technology and pragmatism (which is a quality I self-ascribe, and aspire to, but will admit that I fall short of more often than I'd like.) Children of Gaia seems overall the most decent, tolerant, and humane tribe. But in any case, being a Garou would (for me) be the best.<br /> <br /> As much as I love technology and gadget and the internet, we live in ever more isolated world--and frankly (and I will not get into partisan politics here), it's hard to really <i>believe </i>in any given institution anymore. Being a Garou gives you an immediate, built-in family and fraternity (pack, and to a larger degree Sept; intrigues and machinations notwithstanding). You get the security and comfort of knowing your gods are real, because you can go and commune with them. You get theassurance that your cause is righteous because Gaia is almost cartoonishly/simplistically good, an the Wyrm is (in every conventional, non-&quot;intro to philosophy&quot; moral relativist sense) evil incarnate.<br /> <br /> If every gameline is up against some existential threat and annihilation, I want to play the people who are uniformly trying to do something about it, and who are holding on to their traditions of community and family, and who can still eat, drink, be merry, and love. Also, Garou <i>know</i> there's a heaven. It's not theoretical for them--they can (with great effort) literally go there and be like, &quot;oh word, heaven&quot;.<br /> <br /> I can somewhat understand wanting to be a mage because there's a lot power and <i>options</i> there--they're just human-plus. I can also sorta see wanting to be a changeling (whimsy, fun, adventure, etc.). But I <i>cannot </i>understand why anyone would <i>want</i> to be a vampire, demon, hunter, or wraith. I don't want to be damned, alone, and inevitably spiraling into bestial inhumanity. I also don't want to a ghost constantly fighting the whirlpool of eternal nothingness. I don't want to be a demon constantly fighting back an incalculable amount of time's worth of horrible memories of being in hell. And I don't want to be a hunter because it seems like being a werewolf (i.e., eternal fight against crazy odds), but without the esprit de corp and revelry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T06:15:50-08:00","id":1286673,"title":"","content":"I'd probably be a Gangrel or a Nosferatu who are killed within a week of the Embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T12:07:43-08:00","id":1288025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270535-if-you-have-to-choose-a-splat-which-one-would-you-be?p=1286041#post1286041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to be a demon constantly fighting back an incalculable amount of time's worth of horrible memories of being in hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... but at least i'd <i>look cool</i> while fighting back an incalculable amount of time's worth of horrible memories of being in hell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6149-malfean90","name":"Malfean90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"dat